<task id="070" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Message attachment materialization (ACS/file → SPE → `sprk_document` → intersection); enforce `CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md`</title>
    <phase>W7 — Attachments</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>6</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>020,005</dependencies>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication, spe</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Adds a net-new messaging attachment-materialization step in `Sprk.Bff.Api` that writes to SharePoint Embedded (ADR-007) and creates governed `sprk_document` records + intersection links, and MUST enforce the binding `CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md` (oversize/disallowed rejected). BFF + SPE-touching (publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification); code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W7</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-14</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Materialize a message attachment into Spaarke's channel-agnostic storage model (design §6.4):

    `ACS/file → SPE (SpeFileStore) → sprk_document → sprk_document.sprk_communication lookup + sprk_communicationattachment intersection`.

    A chat file share uploads the binary to SPE, creates the governed `sprk_document`, links it to the message (`sprk_document.sprk_communication` lookup) and to the intersection (`sprk_communicationattachment`), and **the ACS message carries a REFERENCE, not the binary — SPE is the store**. Rendered later as a file card in the timeline (task 060).

    **Reuse the existing `SpeFileStore` facade + the `GraphAttachmentAdapter` shape** — do NOT build a second storage path; the storage SCHEMA is unchanged. The net-new is ONLY the messaging materialization step (email's materialization is email-specific and not behind the archive seam; messaging writes its own step feeding the SAME shape).

    **Enforce `docs/standards/CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md`**: oversize (>25 MB binary) and disallowed MIME types are REJECTED with RFC 7807 ProblemDetails (ADR-019). The policy is the single source of truth — reuse its caps/allow-list; do NOT invent new limits.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication subsystem + SPE integration. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/` (attachment materialization) + `Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs`. Fluent in ADR-007 (SpeFileStore facade — the sole SPE access path), ADR-019 (ProblemDetails), the channel-agnostic `sprk_document` + `sprk_communicationattachment` storage model, `docs/standards/CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md`, §10 BFF Hygiene, §11 Component Justification.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A message attachment materializes into SPE as a governed `sprk_document` linked to the message via `sprk_document.sprk_communication` + the `sprk_communicationattachment` intersection, with the ACS message carrying a reference (not the binary). The materialization reuses `SpeFileStore` + the `GraphAttachmentAdapter` shape (no second storage path, unchanged schema). `CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md` is enforced — oversize/disallowed types are rejected with ProblemDetails. Build clean; materialization + policy-rejection tests pass; publish-size delta + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §6.4 + §2 (current-state): attachment storage is already channel-agnostic — attachment → SPE → `sprk_document` (`sprk_document.sprk_communication` lookup + `sprk_communicationattachment` intersection). But materialization is email-specific and NOT behind the archive seam, so a new channel writes its OWN materialization step feeding the same shape. This task builds that step for messaging. The binary lives in SPE (the store); the ACS message carries only a reference — consistent with "Dataverse is the record, ACS is transport."

      Component Justification (§11): (1) Existing — `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007 SPE facade), the `sprk_document`/`sprk_communicationattachment` model, and the `GraphAttachmentAdapter` shape already exist; this task adds NO new storage entity or SPE path. (2) Extension — a new messaging materialization step reusing the existing SPE facade + adapter shape; storage schema is unchanged. (3) Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete): without the messaging materialization step a chat file share has nowhere governed to land — the attachment is either lost or would (wrongly) be stored as an ACS binary outside Spaarke's document governance (FR-14 acceptance "governed `sprk_document` linked to the message" fails); without policy enforcement an oversize/disallowed file bypasses the binding attachment caps (security/governance failure). Named contract failures, not "future flexibility."

      Policy enforcement: `CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md` is the single source of truth (25 MB binary cap, restrictive MIME allow-list: text/plain, text/markdown, application/pdf, DOCX). Reject oversize/disallowed with RFC 7807 ProblemDetails — do NOT invent new limits or a parallel policy surface. The policy's server gates operate on extracted-text envelopes for chat-with-LLM; this task's binary/MIME gate is the attachment-into-SPE analog — enforce the binary cap + MIME allow-list at materialization.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ (net-new messaging attachment materialization step)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/GraphAttachmentAdapter.cs (materialization shape to reuse — email precedent)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs (ADR-007 SPE facade — the sole SPE access path)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs</file>
      <file>docs/standards/CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md (binding — caps + MIME allow-list to enforce)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-14">Materialize: ACS/file → SPE → `sprk_document` → `sprk_document.sprk_communication` lookup + `sprk_communicationattachment` intersection. The ACS message carries a REFERENCE (not the binary — SPE is the store).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md">Enforce the binding policy: reject oversize (>25 MB binary) + disallowed MIME types (allow-list: text/plain, text/markdown, application/pdf, DOCX). Reuse the policy's caps/allow-list — do NOT invent new limits or a parallel policy.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">All SPE access goes through the `SpeFileStore` facade — the sole SPE access path; MUST NOT bypass it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Oversize/disallowed/failed materialization returns RFC 7807 ProblemDetails.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse `SpeFileStore` + the `GraphAttachmentAdapter` shape; do NOT build a second storage path. Storage SCHEMA unchanged — net-new is ONLY the messaging materialization step.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Inject central `TokenCredential` + canonical Dataverse/Graph interfaces; MUST NOT `new` a credential.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032 / ADR-018">Registration unconditional / Null-Object for any feature-gated dependency; no asymmetric registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Server-side materialization only — MUST NOT introduce a client-side ACS SDK.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§11 Component Justification: state the concrete FR-14 failure modes prevented (ungoverned/lost attachment; policy bypass). §10 bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/plan.md</file>
