      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails-http-standardization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Attachment materialization via SpeFileStore" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/GraphAttachmentAdapter.cs">
        Mirror the email attachment shape: upload binary via `SpeFileStore` → create `sprk_document` → link `sprk_document.sprk_communication` + `sprk_communicationattachment`. Messaging writes its own step feeding the SAME shape; schema unchanged.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Policy gate with ProblemDetails" location="docs/standards/CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md">
        Enforce the binding 25 MB binary cap + MIME allow-list; reject with RFC 7807 ProblemDetails (ADR-019). Reuse the policy's constants/intent — no new limits.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Reference-not-binary" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/">
        The ACS message carries a reference to the SPE `sprk_document`; SPE is the store. Rendered as a file card in the timeline (task 060).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `GraphAttachmentAdapter.cs` (email materialization shape) + `SpeFileStore.cs` (ADR-007 facade) + the task-005 ACS-key columns + `docs/standards/CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md` + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + §11 to identify the exact shape to reuse and the policy caps to enforce.</step>
    <step order="2">Grep to confirm no messaging materialization step exists and that the `sprk_document`/`sprk_communicationattachment` schema needs NO change (§11 existing-question evidence; schema unchanged).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the messaging materialization step: accept the chat file (binary + MIME + filename) + the message context; enforce the policy gate FIRST (binary cap + MIME allow-list) before any upload.</step>
    <step order="4">On pass: upload the binary via `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007 facade only), create the governed `sprk_document`, link `sprk_document.sprk_communication` + create the `sprk_communicationattachment` intersection row; return/record the reference the ACS message carries (not the binary).</step>
    <step order="5">On fail (oversize/disallowed): reject with RFC 7807 ProblemDetails (ADR-019); no SPE upload, no `sprk_document` created.</step>
    <step order="6">Register the materialization step via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional (ADR-032). Confirm no client-side ACS SDK involvement (NFR-04).</step>
    <step order="7">Write tests: (a) a valid file materializes → `sprk_document` created in SPE + `sprk_document.sprk_communication` + `sprk_communicationattachment` linked + reference recorded; (b) POLICY NEGATIVE: an oversize (>25 MB) file is REJECTED with ProblemDetails and NO `sprk_document`/SPE upload occurs; (c) POLICY NEGATIVE: a disallowed MIME type is REJECTED with ProblemDetails; (d) the binary is NOT stored on the ACS message (reference only); (e) all SPE access goes through `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007 — no bypass, diff-verifiable).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing attachment/communication tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0 (reuses existing SPE facade; no new packages).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus policy enforcement + SPE-facade-only + reference-not-binary); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus FR-14, ADR-007 SPE facade, CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY enforcement, §11). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path; shared `Services/Communication/`).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (070 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (materialization entry point, policy-gate placement, reference-recording mechanism).</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Inspect GraphAttachmentAdapter shape, SpeFileStore facade, task-005 ACS keys, the attachment policy</tool>
    <tool name="grep">Confirm no messaging materialization step + schema unchanged (§11 evidence)</tool>
    <tool name="edit">Add the messaging materialization step + policy gate; register in CommunicationModule</tool>
    <tool name="bash">Build, materialization + policy-rejection tests, publish-size, CVE scan</tool>
    <tool name="code-review">FULL-rigor quality gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="adr-check">FULL-rigor quality gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">Pre-PR hot-path conflict scan (Step 10)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ — messaging attachment materialization step (NEW) reusing SpeFileStore + the GraphAttachmentAdapter shape</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs (UPDATED — unconditional registration)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ — materialization happy-path + CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY oversize/disallowed rejection + reference-not-binary + SPE-facade-only tests</output>
    <output type="docs">PR description with §11 Component Justification (FR-14 failure modes) + bff-extensions Placement Justification + publish-size delta + CVE result</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A valid message attachment materializes: binary uploaded via `SpeFileStore`, a governed `sprk_document` created, linked via `sprk_document.sprk_communication` + the `sprk_communicationattachment` intersection, and a reference recorded on the ACS message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The materialization reuses `SpeFileStore` + the `GraphAttachmentAdapter` shape — no second storage path; storage schema unchanged (diff-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The ACS message carries a REFERENCE, not the binary (SPE is the store).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POLICY NEGATIVE: an oversize (>25 MB) file is rejected with RFC 7807 ProblemDetails and NO `sprk_document`/SPE upload occurs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POLICY NEGATIVE: a disallowed MIME type (outside the CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY allow-list) is rejected with ProblemDetails.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All SPE access goes through the `SpeFileStore` facade (ADR-007 — no bypass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Registration is unconditional (ADR-032); no client-side ACS SDK introduced (NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; publish-size delta ≈ 0 vs ~45.30 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 020 (messaging channel provider — the archiver/transcript context) + 005 (ACS-key columns on `sprk_communication`). No `blocks` — an independent W7 track that can run in parallel after W2. The load-bearing correctness properties are (1) policy enforcement BEFORE upload (reject oversize/disallowed early — the negative cases are non-negotiable) and (2) reference-not-binary (SPE is the store; the ACS message never holds the binary). If the storage schema seems to need a change, STOP — the schema is unchanged by design; a needed change signals a mis-shaped materialization step, not a schema gap.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
